The invention concerns a procedure (METH) for determining the distance R separating a vehicle (V) from an identifier (I) used to unlock and start the vehicle (V), where the vehicle (V) and the identifier (I) are synchronized.

The procedure (METH) includes the following operations:

— choosing (Sel_fp) N frequencies fp, with p ∈ [1; N], N being a natural number greater than 3;

— carrying out N sequences Sqp, each sequence Sqp including the following operations:

• sending (Em_Svp), from a transmitter (TXv) of the vehicle (V) to a receiver (RXi) of the identifier (I), a first signal (Svp) having frequency fp;

• determining (Mes_φvip), by means of a processor/calculator (Xi) of the identifier (I), the phase φvip, modulo 2π, of the received first signal (Svp), with respect to a second signal (Sip) whose phase is φip(t)=φ0ip+2πfpt;

• sending (Em_Sip), from a transmitter (TXi) of the identifier (I) to a receiver (RXv) of the vehicle (V), the second signal (Sip);

• determining (Mes_φivp), by means of a processor/calculator (Xv) of the vehicle (V), the phase φivp, modulo 2π, of the received second signal (Sip), with respect to the first signal (Svp);

• computing (Cal_φp) the mean value φp of the phases φvip and φivp;

— for every p from 1 to N−1, computing (Cal_Pp) a slope/ramp Pp according to the relationship Pp = (φp+1 − φp) / (fp+1 − fp); and

— deriving (Cal_R) the distance R from the ramps Pp, where p ∈ [1; N].

